  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Cyclone Montha affected families in Konaseema District</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project, &#x201c;Emergency Response to Cyclone Montha Affected Families in Konaseema District, Andhra Pradesh, India,&#x201d; aims to support 2,500 highly vulnerable households&#x2014;including Dalit, waste picker communities&#x2014;whose homes, assets, and livelihoods were destroyed during the Cyclone. The project will provide multipurpose cash transfers to 2500 affected families to meet immediate needs for food, healthcare, and essential household items, while restoring their dignity and choice. 300 waste pickers out of these 2500 families will receive WASH and Shelter/NFI kits to provide safe living space , to improve hygiene and prevent water borne vector borne diseases. Protection will be mainstreamed in the response and protection awareness will be carried out for sensitising affected communities to identify any protection concern and addressing those.</narrative>
  </description>
